title: Unattended, nobody answers
pid: d0208978-d2e5-4bfb-ad26-a3ed28165cc1
body: |2-
  An agent that runs unattended has no human to approve a command
  the harness asks one about, so such a command hangs it for good:
  one agent sat two hours on 'rm -rf ../../../zt'. Keep temporary
  files under your worktree's 'target/', remove them with 'rm FILE',
  and never 'rm -rf' a path that leaves the worktree or is written
  with '..'. Nor does anyone resume a turn that ends: run the whole
  suite in the foreground (five to fifteen minutes; give the call a
  ten-minute timeout and, if it runs out, wait on the same PID,
  never starting a second run), and do not end your turn while it
  runs.
